
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Makko</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
   

    <header class="page-header">
        <div class="container">
            <h1>Makko Projects</h1>
            <p>A showcase of my programming work and accomplishments</p>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="content-section">
        <div class="projects-carousel-container">
            <button class="carousel-arrow carousel-arrow-left" onclick="previousProject()">‹</button>
            
            <div class="projects-carousel">
                <div class="project-card active">
                    <h3>Project 1: Portal Game</h3>
                    <p class="tech">Python</p>
                    <p class="description">A 2D randomly generated platformer where the user uses portals to move around through the stage.</p>
                    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center; width: 100%;">
                        <iframe width="410" height="460"
                           src="https://academy.cs.cmu.edu/sharing/coralGoldfish016624/embed"> 
                         </iframe>
                    </div>
                    <h4>Challenges & Lessons:</h4>
                    <p>The biggest challenge with this project was the collisions of the player and the world. It was really hard to make the portals work right and not break everything.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="project-card">
                    <h3>Project 2: Endless Shooting Game</h3>
                    <p class="tech">Python</p>
                    <p class="description">A 2D endless shooting game where the enemies get faster over time.</p>
                    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center; width: 100%;">
                        <iframe width="410" height="460"
                           src="https://academy.cs.cmu.edu/sharing/oliveLobster9516/embed"> 
                         </iframe>
                    </div>
                    <h4>Challenges & Lessons:</h4>
                    <p>It was really hard finding a fun, satisfying, and unique way to have the enemies move.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="project-card">
                    <h3>Project 3: 3D Hallway Game</h3>
                    <p class="tech">Python</p>
                    <p class="description">A 3D hallway 50/50 game using a 2D language to make a 3D experience.</p>
                    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center; width: 100%;">
                        <iframe width="410" height="460"
                           src="https://academy.cs.cmu.edu/sharing/goldenrodSpider9820/embed"> 
                         </iframe>
                    </div>
                    <h4>Challenges & Lessons:</h4>
                    <p>It was really hard to get the dimensions right and perspectives of the lines. I also had to make them all move at the appropriate speed in accordance with each other.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="project-card">
                    <h3>Project 4: Pokemon Cynthia Battle</h3>
                    <p class="tech">Python</p>
                    <p class="description">A Pokemon generation 4 champion fight inspired setup simulator where you can cycle through different Pokemon.</p>
                    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center; width: 100%;">
                        <iframe width="410" height="460"
                           src="https://academy.cs.cmu.edu/sharing/thistleSnail1413/embed"> 
                         </iframe>
                    </div>
                    <h4>Challenges & Lessons:</h4>
                    <p>The hardest part of this project was importing the images of the Pokemon and making them the right size.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <button class="carousel-arrow carousel-arrow-right" onclick="nextProject()">›</button>
        </div>
        
        <div class="carousel-indicators">
            <span class="indicator active" onclick="goToProject(0)"></span>
            <span class="indicator" onclick="goToProject(1)"></span>
            <span class="indicator" onclick="goToProject(2)"></span>
            <span class="indicator" onclick="goToProject(3)"></span>
        </div>
    </section>

    <footer>
        <div class="container">
            <p>&copy; 2025 Makko Wankiiri-Hale Computer Science Portfolio. All rights reserved.</p>
            <p>Built with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript | Hosted on GitHub Pages</p>
        </div>
    </footer>

    <script>
        let currentProject = 0;
        const totalProjects = 4;

        function showProject(index) {
            const cards = document.querySelectorAll('.project-card');
            const indicators = document.querySelectorAll('.indicator');
            
            if (index >= totalProjects) {
                currentProject = 0;
            } else if (index < 0) {
                currentProject = totalProjects - 1;
            } else {
                currentProject = index;
            }
            
            cards.forEach(card => card.classList.remove('active'));
            indicators.forEach(indicator => indicator.classList.remove('active'));
            
            cards[currentProject].classList.add('active');
            indicators[currentProject].classList.add('active');
        }

        function nextProject() {
            showProject(currentProject + 1);
        }

        function previousProject() {
            showProject(currentProject - 1);
        }

        function goToProject(index) {
            showProject(index);
        }

        document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
            if (e.key === 'ArrowRight') nextProject();
            if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft') previousProject();
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
